# Context Manifests

Spec: ContextManifests
Purpose:
  Document exactly what was included, excluded, and why.

Schema:
  @context.C<id>
    task:          <task id>
    compiled_at:   <timestamp>
    layers:        [L0, L1, L2]
    included:      [<reference ids>]
    excluded:      [<reference id: reason>]
    budget:
      max_refs:   <n>
      used_refs:  <n>
      max_tokens: <n>
      used_tokens: <n>
    confidence:    HIGH | MEDIUM | LOW
    freshness:     FRESH | STALE | CORRUPT
    contradictions: [<conflict descriptions>]
    version:       v1, v2, ...
    invalidated_by: [<change ids>]

Versioning:
  Context packs are versioned. Changes to dependencies or decisions
  invalidate prior versions.

  C91:v1 → INVALID (D17 changed)
  C91:v2 → ACTIVE

Rules:
  [MAN-01] Every context pack MUST have a manifest.
  [MAN-02] Manifest MUST list exclusions with reasons.
  [MAN-03] Context version MUST increment on dependency change.

Navigation:
  Parent: @../INDEX.sdd
  Compiler: @compiler.sdd

State: +
